            <div xml:id="d243">

                <pb facs="0443" n="129" xml:id="pg129"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/1173</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-11-05T11:30:00+00:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">November 5, 1914, 11:30 a.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5 p.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>992. Your November 3, 8 p.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d243-f1"/>
                    Sir Edward Grey informs me to-day that
                    state of war exists between Great Britain and Turkey. The Turkish Embassy left
                    this morning. I have taken charge of Ottoman interests and directed the Consul
                    General to inform the consuls in the United Kingdom accordingly.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
